# Engineering practices

- One responsibility per function or component. Prefer about 20 lines and two levels of indentation.
- Named exports only for components, hooks, and utils. No `React.FC`. Type props on the function.
- Use a default export only where the framework requires it: Next.js route modules (`page`, `layout`, `loading`, `error`, `not-found`, `template`, `default`) and `src/i18n/request.ts`.
- Prefer derived values. Do not store props or computed data in state.
- In `useEffect`, call a named inner function and list every dependency.
- Keep `try` / `catch` separate from the happy path. Do not return `null` or `undefined` when a clearer type exists.
- Put pure helpers in `src/utils`. Comments explain why, not what.

Details: `docs/frontend/conventions/ENGINEERING.md`
